      {
        "id": 215907,
        "name": "bolnerap",
        "username": "bolnerap",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/bolnerap/{size}/6056_2.png",
        "created_at": "2018-04-03T10:02:54.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Yeah, this one was pretty easy. Infinitor quickly got down to 11, but he stayed there for several rounds until he finally played an AOE card. At several points, I had the board set up so that he would have wiped it easily had he just <span class=\"bbcode-i\">done</span> something. But with all the redirection / damage reduction options, we were in no danger after the heroes' second turns.</p>\n<p>I tried to cheese the Catch a Ride / Reclaim From the Deep / Abject Refugees combo into getting the match overwith earlier, but all I succeeded in doing was getting a couple manifestations off the board a little early. Which was still helpful! But when all my heroes finished between 15 and 22 HP, it didn't ultimately matter.</p>\n<p>MVP was probably Sky-Scraper for dropping double Aggression Modulator on the Thorathian Military in round 2, turning them into a hyper-focused manifestation death squad. But Energy Bracer + Ta Moko + Enduring Intercession was also quite helpful, once I finally got it set up.</p>",
        "post_number": 2,
        "post_type": 1,
